From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 26 16:44:50 1996
From: Farul Ghazali <farul () cuccfa2 ! ccc ! columbia ! edu>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 1996 16:44:50 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Virtual IP addresses for DU3.2b
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621788


Thanks to the 15-20 people that responded to my message. :-)

The original question was:

> Can I configure my Alphaserver to reply to more than one IP address
> through it's one ethernet port? I'm running DEC Unix 3.2b.

The most obvious answer lies in the ifconfig(8) man page which I skimmed
through before I posted, the keyword is alias. 

For example,

ifconfig tu0 128.59.xxx.xxx alias

will activate 128.59.xxx.xxx on the existing interface and

ifconfig tu0 128.59.xxx.xxx delete

will remove it.

Again, much thanks to everyone who answered.

