Regards managers,

I have a strange problem labeling a rz26l with 'disklabel' under 3.2G. A
short recap:

1. 'disklabel -rw rz0 rz26l' produces

"disklabel: ioctl DIOCWDINFO: Open partition would move or shrink
Use alternate partition"

so I hurry along using /dev/rrz0c remembering that this is a common
errormessage when trying to shrink a partition using the default 'rz0'
device. So I do:

2. disklabel -rw /dev/rrz0c rz26l which also fails with the same error.

