Subject: The Solution:  Remote printers
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621658

Hello Everyone,

	Excuse me for not posting the solution to my problem earlier, but I did =
not realize that I was suppose to post the solution.

Well I know that many of you know this information far better than I, =
but in case their is someone out there like myself that is new to DU..  =
This might come in handy.

The original problem:

I needed to set up a remote printer on a DEC-ALPHA running OSF/1 V3.0. =20

The printer model:
Lexmark Optra R=20

What I had done before posting my original question:

 Edited the printcap file and created a spooling directory and created =
an accounting file and error file and have given ownership to daemon.

The printcap entry That I had:

Tech_CO_laser|lp14|lpco|laserco:\
	:lf=3D/usr/adm/lp14err:\
	:lp=3D:/dev/null:\
	:rm=3Dtech_dept_ip:\
	:rp=3Dtech_ip:\
	:sd=3D/usr/spool/lpd14:


The entry in the /etc/hosts file that I had originally:

XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX       tech_dept_ip.leesummit.k12.mo.us       tech_dept

where XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX is the IP address of the printer.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

The people who responded where:

Tom Webster, Bob Berrigan, Bruce Whittaker, Robert Schuhl, Knut Hellebo =
and Darryl Cook

The results below are from the post made by the aforementioned persons.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

The new printcap entry:

Tech_CO_laser|lp14|lpco|laserco:\
        :lf=3D/usr/adm/lp14err:\
        :ct=3Dremote:\
        :lp=3D:\
        :rm=3Dtech_dept_ip:\
        :rp=3Dprinter_cr:\
        :mx#0:\
        :sd=3D/usr/spool/lpd14:\

The new /etc/hosts entry:

XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX       tech_dept_ip.leesummit.k12.mo.us       =
tech_dept_ip

where XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX is the IP address of the printer.



The main changes were:
=09
	Add the ct statement..  :ct=3Dremote:\

	Change rp statemtent to...  rp=3Dprinter_cr

This was defined in the Lexmark manual.

printer_cr adds a carriage return to the end of each line to prevent =
'stair-stepping' by the Optra printer (Thanks Tom Webster)



