Subject: Migrating Ultrix disks to Digital Unix SUMMARY
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621652



Hi all:
Well, as usual, the most definitive answer to my questions came from Dr.
Filesystem, Alan Rollow:


        1.  You can do it that way if you want, but you can also
            just move the disk, run fsck on it and mount it.  Digital
            UNIX supports mounting ULTRIX disks directly.  At some
            point you may want to migrate the data, but you don't
            have to.

        2.  It depends on the version of ULTRIX.  Very old versions
            may not cope with larger than 2 GB file system.  The
            V4 group from about V4.2 to V4.3A cope, but df(1) doesn't
            behave reasonably.  In V4.4 df(1) has been fixed to better
            handle the large file system sizes.  The file size limit
            is still 2 GB, but you can see all the file system.

Most of the folks listed below sent essentially the same info, but
some were under the same misaprehensions I was, ie, that you had to
reformat the drive and that Ultrix NFS could not deal with NFS
partitions over 2Gb.  Both are not true...


