From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 19 07:03:51 1996
From: David Krinsky <krinsky () hcs ! harvard ! edu>
Date: Tue, 19 Nov 1996 07:03:51 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Installing Add'l PCI SCSI Adapters.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621628

The original question:

Could someone please send instructions for how to configure DU 4.0 on an
AlphaStation 233/255 to use an additional SCSI adapter?

The answer:

Reboot using /genvmunix before running doconfig to make a new kernel.

It's that simple, and that counterintuitive.  Thanks to all--this
should be an RTFM, but sadly I only have the docs on CD, which doesn't
always help when one is monkeying around in single-user mode.

For the curious, or manually inclined, the kernel config lines it added:

bus             psiop1     at pci0      slot  12 vector    psiopintr
controller      scsi1      at psiop1    slot  0

