Subject: [SUMMARY] Ping patch
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621547

Thanks to all those who cared to reply. As indicated in fact in previous
messages, particularly the one from Bruce Whittaker:

1) get the ping_plus tar file from 
   ftp://atlanta.service.digital.com/pub/mandatory_upgrades/AXP/OSF1/version

2) copy ALL the files from ./350-248 to /sys/BINARY

3) copy ip_input.o from the upper directory to /sys/BINARY.
   This will replace the ip_input.o that was copied from ./350-248 
   (and IT HAS TO)

4) now do doconfig -c $HOSTNAME

5) everything proceeded smoothly (I am running DU 3.2c)

NOTE: In the install file, they say:
      "copy all the .h files to the proper directory" .... which is not
      totally clear!
      In the ping patch (./350-248) there are 2 .h files:
      socketvar.h and proto_uicp.h
      I found that the 1rst one sits in /usr/sys/include/sys/ and the
      2nd one in  /usr/sys/include/net/
      Not knowing exactly what to do, I recopied those 2 .h files in
      /sys/BINARY _and_ in the above locations before rebuilding the
      kernel.
      Don't know whether this was correct or not, but apparently it
      made no harm.....

Cheers,

