Dear Gurus,

I could not compile xbin ("ftime unresolved")

As indicated by Annette Theissen, Knut Hellebo and Serge Munhoven, the
trick is to put the "-lbsd" flag AFTER the rest (probably I should have
known that):

cc -o xbin xbinunix.c -lbsd

It works. And xbin works also. You don't need to edit a mail and
discard the header (it looks for "This file"). I don't know why, but
I've never been able to have "hexbin" work properly (no line feeds, 
kilomiles-long lines).

For those who are interested, I found xbin from:

ftp.ibp.fr/pub/TeX/CTAN/tools/xbin/xbinunix.c

