From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 12 03:07:29 1996
From: Stephen Pate <pate () nmsnpb ! NMSU ! Edu>
Date: Tue, 12 Nov 1996 03:07:29 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: problem -- can't run batch jobs (fwd)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621484

Hello again!  I only got one response to my request, and it gave the right
answer.  Thanks to Shari Skinner (skinner@zko.dec.com) for the fix.

The problem was that no one could run batch jobs on one of our alphas, even
thought the at.deny and at.allow files were in their proper configuration
(i.e., there was no at.allow file, and the at.deny file as empty).

The solution was to set the permissions of /usr/bin/at to be 

 -rwsr-xr-x	1	root	bin	/usr/bin/at
----^

The "s" permission lets the user have the rights of the owner of the file,
while the file is being run.

							yours,
								Steve Pate

