From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Nov 07 22:19:24 1996
From: Larry Griffith <larry () garfield ! wsc ! mass ! edu>
Date: Thu, 07 Nov 1996 22:19:24 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY]sendmail v8.8.2
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076341621430

Dear Fellow Managers,

	You people are fast!  Several correct responses to my first
query in just minutes.  Thanks to the following:

Respondents
-----------

"Becki S Kain" <bkain1@ford.com>
Juan Gallego <juan@physics.mcgill.ca>
Steve VanDevender <stevev@hexadecimal.uoregon.edu>

Original query
--------------

	I recently installed sendmail v8.8.2 on a network of DEC
3000's running DU v4.0.  Has anyone encountered the following
problems:

	a) I can't seem to turn off VRFY and EXPN requests.  I've
tried both

	O PrivacyOptions=goaway
and	O PrivacyOptions=novrfy,noexpn,authwarnings

in /var/adm/sendmail/sendmail.cf, but sendmail continues to respond to
VRFY and EXPN requests.  Am I doing something stupid or is this a real
problem?

Answer
------

	The former.  You have to have a symbolic link from
/etc/sendmail.cf (which is where sendmail v8.8.2 looks) to
/usr/var/adm/sendmail/sendmail.cf (which is where Digital puts the
configuration).  I knew this and had my server set up correctly, but I
had forgotten the links on the clients.  (Head hanging in shame..)

Second query
------------

	2) I don't distribute aliases via NIS (although I do use NIS
to distribute other maps).  Before this never made a difference, but
with version 8.8.2 I had to take yp out of the line

	aliases=local,yp

in /etc/svc.conf.  Otherwise sendmail would complain loudly and
frequently about non-existent NIS maps in the mail.log file.  Has
anyone else observed this?

Answer
------

	None yet.  (Actually this is just for information; as
indicated I was able to workaround the problem by changing
/etc/svc.conf.)  If I hear anything I'll summarize.

							Larry

