I originally had the following problem:

> Hi. I have installed the patches for the ping problem on DU 3.2c and
> now instead of simply causing a machine reboot, I get a:
> trap: invalid memory write acess from Kernel mode
> panic. I installed patch 350-248 prior to copying in the new ip_input.o
> file, then rebuilt and booted the new kernel. I am wondering if others
> have had any success applying these patches to a 3.2c system. I'm hoping
> that something is wrong with the system I tested on rather than their
> being a problem with the patches. I'll summarize.

After getting the time to delve back into this problem, I found that
it was indeed an operator headspace problem. Basically, I forgot to 
apply the correct ip_input.o patch. I had applied the patch 350-248
and copied the same ip_input.o patch again. So, the ping problem is
gone on this 3000 tc machine. I will apply it to the remaining 
workstations tomorrow night. 

